# Copy to .dev.vars for local `wrangler dev` (.dev.vars is gitignored).
# In production these are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>` — they are NOT
# in wrangler.jsonc. Public IDs (GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GITHUB_CLIENT_ID,
# ADMIN_EMAILS, VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY) already live in wrangler.jsonc "vars".

# Signs/verifies session cookies AND OAuth-state tokens. Any long random string.
SESSION_SECRET=""

# Google OAuth — console.cloud.google.com > Credentials > OAuth 2.0 Client ID.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# GitHub OAuth — github.com/settings/developers > OAuth Apps.
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Web Push (VAPID). Generate with: npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# The public half is VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY in wrangler.jsonc; keep the pair in sync.
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=""
# mailto: address or site URL identifying the push sender, e.g. mailto:you@example.com
VAPID_SUBJECT=""
